WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.911 --> 00:00:03.673
Journey into the dark side of the soul.

00:00:07.859 --> 00:00:09.861
Into the nightmare world of Mafia Hitman.

00:00:12.923 --> 00:00:17.669
Learn the secret to violent madness as you probe the minds of the killers from the underworld.

00:00:54.713 --> 00:00:54.853
They

00:00:54.894 --> 00:00:57.835
may be international syndicates or inner-city street gangs.

00:00:58.715 --> 00:01:02.435
Their criminal activities can range from drug smuggling to white-collar scams.

00:01:03.472 --> 00:01:06.534
Regardless of the illicit enterprise culture or sphere of power,

00:01:07.335 --> 00:01:10.557
the chief currency of all underworld empires is death.

00:01:11.478 --> 00:01:15.500
For the history of organized crime is a history soaked in blood.

00:01:17.542 --> 00:01:19.222
A blood-drenched tide is rising.

00:01:20.764 --> 00:01:22.525
Violence and death flood our cities.

00:01:23.186 --> 00:01:24.867
The homicide rate is escalating.

00:01:26.147 --> 00:01:27.609
For killers walk among us.

00:01:29.189 --> 00:01:30.109
They look like anyone.

00:01:30.730 --> 00:01:31.932
Professional assassins.

00:01:32.795 --> 00:01:33.676
Sexual sadists,

00:01:34.796 --> 00:01:36.156
nomadic serial killers.

00:01:38.257 --> 00:01:40.337
Chances are you may meet one someday.

00:01:41.237 --> 00:01:43.838
You could pass a psychopathic person on the street,

00:01:44.098 --> 00:01:44.718
even a killer,

00:01:45.238 --> 00:01:46.280
and not really know it.

00:01:46.759 --> 00:01:50.441
Although I have met some psychopathic killers who've killed a lot of people,

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:53.581
who have that so-called reptilian stare,

00:01:53.762 --> 00:01:57.662
where there's a cold iciness that you feel when you sit with them,

00:01:57.682 --> 00:01:59.462
because you know that there's just nothing there.

00:01:59.962 --> 00:02:00.442
Many of them,

00:02:00.483 --> 00:02:02.183
particularly more sophisticated ones.

00:02:02.795 --> 00:02:05.477
can put on a chameleon-like exterior,

00:02:05.617 --> 00:02:07.239
which is superficially glib,

00:02:07.780 --> 00:02:09.100
engaging and charming,

00:02:09.701 --> 00:02:13.685
disarming everyday people from realizing what they're sitting with.

00:02:14.045 --> 00:02:19.009
Psychologist Chris Monhandy is a criminal profiler for the Los Angeles Police Department.

00:02:19.909 --> 00:02:23.834
The people that I've talked to that are of this psychopathic killer variety,

00:02:24.394 --> 00:02:28.858
when they relay their stories of the details of their crimes and how they killed people,

00:02:28.957 --> 00:02:29.679
hunted people,

00:02:30.138 --> 00:02:31.039
and harmed people...

00:02:32.004 --> 00:02:37.546
There is not one bit of remorse in the hardened ones that I've talked with,

00:02:37.747 --> 00:02:42.370
the ones that have made a repetitive venture of hunting and killing people.

00:02:43.210 --> 00:02:43.790
There is a,

00:02:44.831 --> 00:02:46.252
when you talk with them about the killing,

00:02:46.792 --> 00:02:50.454
it's as if they're talking about what they had for dinner the night before.

00:02:52.515 --> 00:02:54.496
John Yarborough is a criminal profiler.

00:02:55.037 --> 00:02:59.058
He uses psychology to build personality profiles of possible suspects.

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:01.140
His specialty?

00:03:01.868 --> 00:03:02.707
The sex murder.

00:03:03.588 --> 00:03:06.750
And I don't mean to create panic in anybody,

00:03:06.890 --> 00:03:16.092
but the reality is there are these sexual predators that no endless amount of incarceration is going to deter.

00:03:16.412 --> 00:03:17.773
They are going to do this.

00:03:18.913 --> 00:03:24.754
University of California neuroscientist Adrian Rain is probing the brains of violent criminals.

00:03:25.995 --> 00:03:28.096
This is an MRI which...

00:03:28.475 --> 00:03:30.717
shows that the brain of a violent individual,

00:03:30.777 --> 00:03:35.381
we can literally cut inside the brains of violent offenders using this technique.

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:36.521
It's non-invasive,

00:03:36.581 --> 00:03:39.424
there's no pain or anything like that,

00:03:39.503 --> 00:03:47.189
but it's a technique which allows us to look with exquisite detail at the structure of the brain of the violent offender.

00:03:47.729 --> 00:03:49.471
Probe inside the brain of a killer.

00:03:50.151 --> 00:03:53.313
Psychoanalyze the mind of a sex murderer.

00:03:53.314 --> 00:03:54.715
Years ago this would be absurd.

00:03:55.235 --> 00:03:55.795
No longer.

00:03:57.360 --> 00:04:02.742
Today researchers and criminologists are at the threshold of answering questions that have long tormented society.

00:04:04.084 --> 00:04:08.385
Why are we the only animal who finds joy in torturing and killing our own kind?

00:04:12.027 --> 00:04:15.030
What forces transform a person into a lord of death?

00:04:16.831 --> 00:04:18.632
What motivates her violent madness?

00:04:19.992 --> 00:04:22.194
Who are the killers who walk among us?

00:04:22.754 --> 00:04:23.975
We can get people who,

00:04:24.975 --> 00:04:25.776
to the extreme...

00:04:27.104 --> 00:04:27.704
are cunning,

00:04:28.265 --> 00:04:28.745
clever,

00:04:29.345 --> 00:04:30.366
manipulative,

00:04:30.746 --> 00:04:31.987
they're very charismatic,

00:04:32.787 --> 00:04:35.569
but they don't care an iota about the victims.

00:04:36.049 --> 00:04:38.531
They have no empathy for the victims,

00:04:38.532 --> 00:04:40.752
they have no remorse for the crimes they've committed.

00:04:41.375 --> 00:04:42.456
And they're motivated by thrill.

00:04:42.956 --> 00:04:44.897
And that's the classic psychopath.

00:04:45.538 --> 00:04:48.900
They usually look at everyday citizen as just kind of this inert,

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:50.161
neutral.

00:04:51.642 --> 00:04:53.603
They would look at them as the sheep that are out there,

00:04:54.624 --> 00:04:59.227
that are pawns in their war against the system.

00:05:00.427 --> 00:05:02.789
Their fury has reached our neighborhoods and homes.

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:05.070
Drive-by shootings,

00:05:05.210 --> 00:05:05.991
home invasions.

00:05:07.599 --> 00:05:10.060
In the ultra-violent new world of organized crime,

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:11.261
everyone is vulnerable.

00:05:13.002 --> 00:05:13.702
In the old days,

00:05:13.842 --> 00:05:16.104
if two of us beat up one of you,

00:05:16.964 --> 00:05:19.806
you and your group could or could not retaliate.

00:05:19.807 --> 00:05:21.507
It was pretty much an option for you.

00:05:22.467 --> 00:05:25.269
But if two of us shoot and kill one of yours,

00:05:25.869 --> 00:05:30.431
the demand character of that situation is such that you are almost bound and determined,

00:05:31.092 --> 00:05:31.932
somebody in your group,

00:05:32.172 --> 00:05:34.294
to try and repay that event,

00:05:35.014 --> 00:05:36.675
to fire back at some point.

00:05:37.099 --> 00:05:38.100
Maybe not successfully,

00:05:38.120 --> 00:05:41.221
but the requirement to do so is much greater than it used to be.

00:05:41.441 --> 00:05:45.084
So the homicide cycles on itself didn't used to be the case.

00:05:47.685 --> 00:05:47.805
Well,

00:05:47.806 --> 00:05:49.026
it didn't get violent until the 80s.

00:05:49.027 --> 00:05:49.206
Well,

00:05:49.226 --> 00:05:49.806
I can tell you,

00:05:49.826 --> 00:05:52.588
I came into this detail in 1972,

00:05:52.768 --> 00:05:53.788
and it was violent then.

00:05:54.349 --> 00:05:57.170
The difference is they had junk guns in those days.

00:05:57.171 --> 00:05:59.452
They didn't have necessarily good guns.

00:06:00.132 --> 00:06:01.653
Sawed-off shotguns and

00:06:02.373 --> 00:06:05.295
.22s, where now they all have excellent weaponry.

00:06:05.859 --> 00:06:08.821
A new 9mm or .380 tends to be their favorite weapon,

00:06:08.841 --> 00:06:11.142
and you put a lot of bullets in the air with one of those.

00:06:11.963 --> 00:06:12.383
All of a sudden,

00:06:12.403 --> 00:06:14.884
now y'all is into it because of the drugs.

00:06:15.405 --> 00:06:15.705
You know,

00:06:15.785 --> 00:06:18.006
now either he want to kill you or you want to kill him.

00:06:18.007 --> 00:06:19.167
Either he's behind,

00:06:19.187 --> 00:06:20.087
he want to jack you,

00:06:21.068 --> 00:06:22.229
or he want this neighborhood,

00:06:22.949 --> 00:06:24.090
or you want the neighborhood.

00:06:24.830 --> 00:06:26.431
So everybody want to be Scarface.

00:06:27.492 --> 00:06:28.532
Crips killing Crips.

00:06:29.173 --> 00:06:30.193
Crips killing Bloods.

00:06:30.253 --> 00:06:31.294
Bloods killing Bloods.

00:06:31.394 --> 00:06:32.074
Bloods killing

00:06:32.475 --> 00:06:32.815
Crips.

00:06:33.331 --> 00:06:34.552
The thing just went haywire.

00:06:34.553 --> 00:06:38.333
The drugs came in and had everybody going crazy.

00:06:40.954 --> 00:06:41.735
It's all negative.

00:06:43.935 --> 00:06:46.557
Gangland murder has evolved into mafia terrorism.

00:06:49.278 --> 00:06:50.358
Our homes are stormed,

00:06:50.378 --> 00:06:54.320
our families brutalized by ethnic gangs who live by their code of death.

00:06:55.540 --> 00:06:55.680
Well,

00:06:55.700 --> 00:06:59.802
within these Chinese gangs and the Vietnamese gangs for that matter,

00:07:00.962 --> 00:07:02.043
home invasions are...

00:07:03.183 --> 00:07:04.804
A common place.

00:07:04.844 --> 00:07:07.004
First thing they do when they burst into a home,

00:07:08.945 --> 00:07:10.365
if the head of the family,

00:07:10.366 --> 00:07:11.425
the male person is present,

00:07:11.486 --> 00:07:12.866
they shoot that person in the leg.

00:07:20.468 --> 00:07:21.648
We know you've got the money

00:07:23.249 --> 00:07:25.550
Leave me the money now Where's the money?

00:07:25.570 --> 00:07:29.911
Shut up Give me the money

00:07:38.435 --> 00:07:40.836
Another technique they use if a very small child,

00:07:40.896 --> 00:07:41.577
preferably a baby,

00:07:41.578 --> 00:07:42.077
is present,

00:07:42.497 --> 00:07:43.338
they take the baby...

00:07:43.339 --> 00:07:48.040
No No

00:07:54.264 --> 00:07:57.285
No ...and they tape it to the wall using electrical duct tape.

00:07:57.286 --> 00:08:02.929
They then take their weapon and they fire shots around the wall.

00:08:05.570 --> 00:08:06.851
A bit like a Bugs Bunny cartoon.

00:08:07.471 --> 00:08:08.591
A little bit more dangerous.

00:08:09.612 --> 00:08:15.695
The wholesale slaughter by today's gangbangers is far different than how the mafia once fulfilled their bloodlust.

00:08:18.596 --> 00:08:21.857
Lucky Luciano once boasted that the mob only kills each other.

00:08:22.678 --> 00:08:26.179
Killing outside the ranks of organized crime would only bring down the heat,

00:08:26.439 --> 00:08:26.980
they reasoned.

00:08:28.680 --> 00:08:29.441
Politicians,

00:08:29.521 --> 00:08:30.301
public servants,

00:08:30.302 --> 00:08:31.161
the average citizen,

00:08:31.602 --> 00:08:33.743
they were all off-limits to mob hitmen.

00:08:34.947 --> 00:08:38.808
The transformation of the Mafia into an organization with enforcement rules,

00:08:39.048 --> 00:08:40.209
recruitment procedures,

00:08:40.229 --> 00:08:46.070
and a managerial hierarchy occurred when the fabric of America was undergoing a major alteration.

00:08:49.111 --> 00:08:50.552
It was the Industrial Age.

00:08:51.612 --> 00:08:54.833
A fresh breeze whistled through the skyscrapers of American business.

00:08:56.774 --> 00:09:00.335
New theories on labor productivity and management were picking up steam.

00:09:01.855 --> 00:09:06.577
Mom-and-pop stores and shops fell victim to the consolidation and growth of national firms.

00:09:08.058 --> 00:09:10.038
A new species of American was born,

00:09:11.079 --> 00:09:11.979
the corporate man,

00:09:13.080 --> 00:09:16.761
a loyal worker who rose to prominence by simply following orders.

00:09:18.142 --> 00:09:22.103
It's been said organized crime is a twisted image of the society it preys on,

00:09:23.784 --> 00:09:28.026
and mob kingpins were quick to embrace the new business idea as a specialization,

00:09:28.346 --> 00:09:29.626
marketing and merging.

00:09:31.479 --> 00:09:36.662
Godfather's Lucky Luciano and Meyer Lansky consolidated the mob into a national syndicate.

00:09:38.383 --> 00:09:40.944
They decided to market one of their principal resources,

00:09:41.985 --> 00:09:42.645
mob gunmen,

00:09:43.406 --> 00:09:44.867
masters of killing and torture.

00:09:47.375 --> 00:09:48.736
The enterprise was called

00:09:49.256 --> 00:09:50.596
Murder Incorporated.

00:09:53.537 --> 00:09:54.877
The business plan was simple.

00:09:55.918 --> 00:09:59.059
Acquire an elite stable of killers whose job description was

00:09:59.419 --> 00:10:00.599
Mafia Hitman.

00:10:01.639 --> 00:10:06.261
Any crime group associated with the syndicate could purchase a service as a Murder Incorporated.

00:10:07.001 --> 00:10:09.641
The reigning godfathers must approve all killings.

00:10:10.282 --> 00:10:13.082
Payment would always be made before the murder was completed.

00:10:13.823 --> 00:10:14.963
After the job was done,

00:10:15.427 --> 00:10:17.268
The hitmen would receive a new assignment.

00:10:18.268 --> 00:10:18.728
For years,

00:10:18.748 --> 00:10:20.609
there had been rumors of such an operation.

00:10:21.309 --> 00:10:24.770
But most refused to believe that a death squad could be working in America.

00:10:25.910 --> 00:10:27.311
But in 1939,

00:10:27.312 --> 00:10:33.092
disbelief was shot full of holes when one of murdering corporate's top enforcers took the stand.

00:10:36.734 --> 00:10:38.554
It was a murder trial of a mob killer.

00:10:43.843 --> 00:10:46.964
A highly placed enforcer called Kid Twist had turned informant.

00:10:50.466 --> 00:10:51.186
Abe Rellis'

00:10:51.266 --> 00:10:54.968
testimony opened the public's eye to the evil that was murder incorporated.

00:10:58.309 --> 00:11:00.130
Mobsters were not pleased.

00:11:01.091 --> 00:11:02.631
You open your mouth and you're a dead man,

00:11:02.731 --> 00:11:02.991
kid.

00:11:03.632 --> 00:11:04.492
I swear I'll bleed for myself.

00:11:04.532 --> 00:11:08.634
You're squealing,

00:11:08.654 --> 00:11:09.094
you're dead.

00:11:17.291 --> 00:11:19.172
Mafia bosses enact their codes,

00:11:19.392 --> 00:11:20.113
achieve goals,

00:11:20.133 --> 00:11:22.194
and maintain control through enforcers,

00:11:22.754 --> 00:11:24.696
wise guys who take care of contracts.

00:11:25.756 --> 00:11:25.996
In the

00:11:26.597 --> 00:11:27.737
1930s, they were called the muscle.

00:11:28.798 --> 00:11:30.739
When Murder Incorporated was established,

00:11:31.039 --> 00:11:32.440
mob muscle became a business.

00:11:33.461 --> 00:11:39.344
Never in the history of crime had murder become such an organized enterprise as it did with Murder Incorporated.

00:11:41.105 --> 00:11:43.407
Kid Twist knew where all the bodies were buried.

00:11:44.127 --> 00:11:46.468
Told of hundreds of killings by mob enforcers,

00:11:46.748 --> 00:11:51.729
fingering godfathers like Lucky Luciano and sadistic gunman Frank Abbandondo.

00:11:55.450 --> 00:11:56.350
For the first time,

00:11:56.351 --> 00:11:58.071
the deadly language of the mob was heard.

00:11:58.951 --> 00:12:00.752
Orders for killings were contracts,

00:12:01.192 --> 00:12:02.292
hits were murders,

00:12:03.172 --> 00:12:05.633
and the victim was always known as the bum.

00:12:06.433 --> 00:12:07.013
For the record,

00:12:07.033 --> 00:12:07.453
Your Honor,

00:12:07.454 --> 00:12:09.294
the witnesses pointed out the defendant,

00:12:09.334 --> 00:12:09.554
Mr.

00:12:09.594 --> 00:12:10.774
Frank Abbandondo,

00:12:11.154 --> 00:12:13.055
also known as the Dasher.

00:12:13.619 --> 00:12:13.819
Now,

00:12:14.379 --> 00:12:15.620
according to your testimony,

00:12:15.700 --> 00:12:16.080
Mr.

00:12:16.140 --> 00:12:16.480
Ellis,

00:12:17.340 --> 00:12:17.560
Mr.

00:12:17.580 --> 00:12:20.081
Robin Dondo's committed over 45 murders,

00:12:20.082 --> 00:12:20.721
is that correct?

00:12:21.061 --> 00:12:21.201
Yeah,

00:12:21.202 --> 00:12:22.581
the Dasher was always busy.

00:12:23.422 --> 00:12:24.802
He may have even knocked out more.

00:12:25.362 --> 00:12:27.083
He was getting contracts all the time.

00:12:27.503 --> 00:12:28.383
He loved his job.

00:12:28.703 --> 00:12:29.543
Where would you and,

00:12:30.204 --> 00:12:32.664
the Dasher receive your orders,

00:12:32.764 --> 00:12:32.984
your,

00:12:33.805 --> 00:12:34.465
contracts?

00:12:34.685 --> 00:12:36.505
All of us guys hung around Midnight Roses.

00:12:36.925 --> 00:12:37.566
You know the place,

00:12:37.567 --> 00:12:38.666
the candy store in Brooklyn?

00:12:39.666 --> 00:12:40.847
Roses is where we got our orders.

00:12:41.507 --> 00:12:42.527
We went all over the country.

00:12:43.487 --> 00:12:46.708
Now the boss only gave us contracts to places we've never been before.

00:12:47.129 --> 00:12:48.709
And that was the beauty of the operation.

00:12:49.129 --> 00:12:50.270
We go into some town,

00:12:50.650 --> 00:12:51.310
we hit the bum,

00:12:51.330 --> 00:12:52.651
and then we take the next train out.

00:12:53.891 --> 00:12:55.032
Cops always look for a motive,

00:12:55.033 --> 00:12:56.092
but with an unknown killer,

00:12:56.352 --> 00:12:57.013
there was none.

00:12:57.993 --> 00:12:59.534
Guys were coming and going all the time.

00:12:59.874 --> 00:13:01.575
We were the doing hits or dumping bodies.

00:13:02.035 --> 00:13:03.235
Guys like Michael Capone.

00:13:03.936 --> 00:13:04.496
Trigger Mike,

00:13:04.497 --> 00:13:05.056
we called him.

00:13:05.776 --> 00:13:08.258
He had his wife murdered in a hospital bed after she gave birth.

00:13:08.878 --> 00:13:09.578
He felt bad,

00:13:09.618 --> 00:13:09.778
though.

00:13:10.018 --> 00:13:11.559
Always wished he had done the hit himself.

00:13:12.443 --> 00:13:13.224
Happy Malone.

00:13:13.884 --> 00:13:14.485
Called him Happy.

00:13:14.685 --> 00:13:17.767
He's always laughing and giggling every time he's killing someone.

00:13:17.768 --> 00:13:18.608
Vito Garini.

00:13:19.189 --> 00:13:21.511
He kept his tomb by shooting the heads off chickens.

00:13:22.031 --> 00:13:23.112
So we called him Chickenhead.

00:13:24.053 --> 00:13:24.913
Pittsburgh Phil.

00:13:25.354 --> 00:13:25.934
Called him Pep.

00:13:25.935 --> 00:13:27.656
He held the top score for kills.

00:13:28.376 --> 00:13:29.737
Over 60.

00:13:29.757 --> 00:13:30.018
Yeah,

00:13:30.738 --> 00:13:32.239
those guys are the best in the country.

00:13:33.541 --> 00:13:34.221
Bring it across.

00:13:35.002 --> 00:13:36.923
And this organization,

00:13:37.924 --> 00:13:39.425
Murder Incorporated,

00:13:40.426 --> 00:13:41.327
whose idea was it?

00:13:42.003 --> 00:13:43.444
All the bosses had their hands in it,

00:13:43.845 --> 00:13:46.287
but it was Louis Lepke and Luciano's idea.

00:13:46.787 --> 00:13:47.128
You see,

00:13:47.428 --> 00:13:48.989
Lucky got where he is by killing people,

00:13:49.189 --> 00:13:49.630
and Lepke,

00:13:49.730 --> 00:13:49.930
well,

00:13:50.210 --> 00:13:51.451
he just liked to hurt people too.

00:13:52.633 --> 00:13:52.853
Yeah,

00:13:53.533 --> 00:13:54.494
murdering was their baby,

00:13:54.574 --> 00:13:54.895
all right.

00:13:57.457 --> 00:14:00.960
Louis Lepke and the formidable Luciano cultivated a charming,

00:14:01.040 --> 00:14:02.241
sophisticated image.

00:14:03.422 --> 00:14:04.143
In reality,

00:14:05.124 --> 00:14:08.807
Luciano and Lepke's first solution to any problem was violent aggression.

00:14:10.635 --> 00:14:16.738
The decision to push the power of mafia families by establishing Murder Incorporated was instinctive for men who,

00:14:16.878 --> 00:14:17.598
under the skin,

00:14:18.038 --> 00:14:19.479
were pure psychopaths.

00:14:20.539 --> 00:14:25.021
Now what typically will happen is in these families you'll have kind of a leader,

00:14:27.042 --> 00:14:28.182
you'll definitely have a leader,

00:14:28.802 --> 00:14:30.623
